# The build context is what the two Dockerfiles copy and nothing else. It is sent to the builder
# whole, so anything let in travels with it: a `.env`, a development database, a key, a backup or
# a restore's leftovers, under whatever name Routarr writes next. A file a Dockerfile starts
# copying needs its line here (`scripts/tests/test_ignored.py`).
*
!LICENSE
!backend/Cargo.toml
!backend/Cargo.lock
!backend/about.toml
!backend/about.hbs
!backend/migrations/
!backend/locales/
!backend/src/
!backend/rust-toolchain.toml
!frontend/

# Inside what is copied: rebuilt in the image, or a secret.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/coverage/
frontend/test-results/
**/.env
